-- ============================================================================
-- 226_qa_sheet_layouts_from_client_files.sql
--
-- Puts the client's own sheets in front of reviewers, instead of waiting for a
-- manager to open Scorecards & Config and press "Load". Same layouts, same
-- source: this file is GENERATED from frontend/src/utils/qaSheetPresets.js by
--
--   node backend/tools/gen_qa_preset_sql.mjs \
--        closer_dispo=553dc454-0a67-4570-9181-ebbccf37b633 \
--        tra=7ac05eba-4787-40ed-9f8b-c7f238301d6f
--
-- so the sheet a reviewer scores and the layout that button loads cannot drift.
-- Re-run the generator and regenerate this file if a layout changes; do not
-- hand-edit the JSON below.
--
-- WHAT CHANGES
--
-- closer_dispo 553dc454 "Closer — Unclosed Sale" — 22 fill-in columns plus the
--   computed Closer_Base_Score = the 23 columns of "unclosed sample.xlsx", in
--   the file's order and spelling ("Callbak Date" is theirs). Call Status is the
--   reviewer's Pass/Fail verdict, Call Outcome is Closed / Callback / No
--   Conversation (the file's one-word spelling — the closer_disposition
--   auto-fill is an EXACT match, so the spelling decides whether it self-fills),
--   Wrong Dispo keeps the file's Yes/No. Base divides by 25 (5 ratings × max 5).
--
-- tra 7ac05eba "WaveTech Fronter — TRA" — replaced wholesale, because
--   "TRA for scorecard.xlsx" is a different scoring model, not a revision: six
--   WEIGHTED columns picked from their own band lists (0/5/10 · 0/5/10/15/20 ·
--   0/5/10/15), summed exactly as the file's =G+H+I+J+K+L. The bands are the
--   file's and total 95, so the divisor is 100 and Base_Score prints the number
--   the sheet's Score column prints (75 → 75.0%, perfect call 95%). Final Status
--   is a manual Pass/Fail and is authoritative; Status (Standard / Below
--   Standard) is captured but never moves the score. The old 0–4 ratings,
--   auto-fails and penalties go with the sheet they came from.
--
-- HISTORY: nothing is deleted. Column KEYS are the ones these cards already use
-- wherever the layouts share a column, so qa_review_scores rows stay attached.
-- TRA's six weighted columns are genuinely new keys, so the 4 reviews on the old
-- 0–4 columns keep their rows but no longer have a column on the sheet — that is
-- unavoidable when the client replaces the sheet.
--
-- Apply AFTER 225 (which leaves exactly one active global card per method).
--
-- Verify — expect 22 and 18, and sheet_v2 on both:
--   SELECT method, criteria->>'model' AS model,
--          jsonb_array_length(criteria->'fields') AS columns,
--          criteria->>'base_score_divisor' AS divisor
--     FROM qa_scorecards
--    WHERE id IN ('553dc454-0a67-4570-9181-ebbccf37b633',
--                 '7ac05eba-4787-40ed-9f8b-c7f238301d6f');
-- ============================================================================

